{"text":"Owen cuts his 54-inch ribbon into 6 equal portions to use in a project. Each piece is 9 inches. He wants to use a piece that is 3 times as long for a bigger marker. How many inches would that piece be?"}

Owen cuts a 54-inch ribbon into 6 equal portions. Each portion is 54 divided by 6, which equals 9 inches. He wants to use a piece that is 3 times as long as one of these 9-inch pieces. Multiply 9 by 3 to find the length of the longer piece. 9 times 3 equals 27. The piece he wants to use would be 27 inches long.
#### 27

{"question":"Clara has 4 hives. Each hive gives 7 jars of honey. She sells each jar for £4. How much does she earn in total?"}

Clara has 4 hives. Each hive produces 7 jars of honey. Multiply the number of hives by the number of jars per hive: 4 × 7 = 28 jars. Each jar is sold for £4. Multiply the total number of jars by the price per jar: 28 × 4 = 112. Clara earns £112 in total.
#### 112
